=== add-apt-repository ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Only ONE of -P, -C, -U, -S, or old-style 'line' can be specified


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  add-apt-repository [-h] [-d] [-r] [-s] [-c COMPONENT] [-p POCKET] [-y]
      [-n] [-l] [--dry-run] [-L] [-P PPA] [-C CLOUD] [-U URI] [-S
      SOURCESLIST [SOURCESLIST ...]] [line ...]


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  line...  sources.list line to add (deprecated)


FLAGS (15) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-h, --help           show this help message and exit
-d, --debug          Print debug
-r, --remove         Disable repository
-s, --enable-source  Allow downloading of the source packages from the
                     repository
-c, --component COMPONENT Components to use with the repository
-p, --pocket POCKET  Add entry for this pocket
-y, --yes            Assume yes to all queries
-n, --no-update      Do not update package cache after adding
-l, --login          Login to Launchpad.
    --dry-run        Don't actually make any changes.
-L, --list           List currently configured repositories
-P, --ppa PPA        PPA to add
-C, --cloud CLOUD    Cloud Archive to add
-U, --uri URI        Archive URI to add
-S, --sourceslist SOURCESLIST [SOURCESLIST ...] Full sources.list entry line
                     to add
